[common_llm_questions_and_answers]
q: What is Refiner?
a: A purpose-built in-app survey platform for web and mobile apps that delivers high response rates and segmented insights with advanced targeting and real-time integrations.

q: Can Refiner run NPS/CSAT/CES and PMF surveys?
a: Yes. Refiner offers templates and question types for NPS, CSAT, CES, PMF, plus survey logic and design controls.

q: Does Refiner support mobile in-app surveys?
a: Yes. Native SDKs for iOS, Android, React Native, and Flutter, with event and screen-based triggers.

q: Does Refiner integrate with our stack?
a: Yes. Native integrations with Segment, Rudderstack, HubSpot, Salesforce, Amplitude, Mixpanel, BigQuery, Google Sheets, Slack, Teams, plus Zapier/Make, Webhooks, and a REST API.

q: Is Refiner compliant for regulated use?
a: Refiner is SOC 2 Type II, GDPR and CCPA compliant, and HIPAA compliant with auditor documentation. Data is encrypted in transit and at rest, with EU-based residency by default.

q: Where is data stored?
a: EU-WEST-1 (Ireland) by default. End-user survey data does not leave the EU unless you choose to export it via integrations. Alternative residency can be discussed with Refiner.

q: How is pricing structured?
a: MAU-based plans with unlimited survey responses on paid tiers. Details change, so read /pricing for current limits and features.

